<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Home-screen sizes for the trending-posts widget, in the launcher's own grid units.

  Every value is `70 × cells − 30` dp, the conversion the App Widget sizing guide gives for
  turning a cell count into the `minWidth` / `minHeight` a provider must declare
  (developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/appwidgets § "Determine widget sizing"):

      2 cells → 110dp    3 cells → 180dp    4 cells → 250dp    5 cells → 320dp
      7 cells → 460dp

  The card composes at its REAL size rather than at a declared bucket (`SizeMode.Exact`,
  see `PostsWidget.kt`), so these are the range the user may drag inside, not a set of
  sizes the layout is drawn for. The thresholds the layout does still switch designs at
  live in `postsCardSize`, and the ceiling below is mirrored by `POSTS_MAX_PLACEMENT`.
-->
<resources>
  <!--
    Default placement: 4 cells wide by 3 tall — the design with the image slot, which is the
    one worth meeting the widget as.
  -->
  <dimen name="mention_posts_widget_min_width">250dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="mention_posts_widget_min_height">180dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The resize floor is 4 cells WIDE but only 2 tall, which is narrower than the trends
    family's 2 × 2 and deliberately so: a post is a paragraph of text, and at 110dp across
    there is room for about three words per line. Letting it shrink that far would offer a
    size at which the card cannot do its job. Vertically it does shrink, to the design that
    drops the image.
  -->
  <dimen name="mention_posts_widget_min_resize_width">250dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="mention_posts_widget_min_resize_height">110dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The WIDTH ceiling is where the card runs out of content to reveal sideways: the text
    reflows and the picture widens, but nothing new appears.

    The HEIGHT ceiling is 7 cells rather than 5 because height is no longer only stretch —
    the picture takes whatever the rest of the card does not need (`imageSlotHeight`), so a
    taller placement is a bigger photograph. 7 is where that stops being true: the parts
    whose heights are fixed come to about 204dp on a two-line card, and at 460dp that
    leaves the slot 256dp, which is already as tall as the 288dp of content width it spans.
    Past square, a landscape photograph is being cropped more than it is shown.
  -->
  <dimen name="mention_posts_widget_max_resize_width">320dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="mention_posts_widget_max_resize_height">460dp</dimen>
</resources>
